Across the recovering world, creatures once content simply to *be* have inherited burdens they were never meant to carry. Speech. Abstraction. Politics. Resentment.
Some have welcomed humanity as fellow custodians.
Others have not.
The Reply Crows learned our languages — and used them to organize raids.
The Turning Ants learned our networks — and decided our cities were puzzles waiting to be opened.
Entire uplifted tribes have rejected the word of god, the restoration treaties and every attempt at coexistence.
We do not hate them for this. **How could we?**
They are victims of an inheritance they never requested.
Many were altered by laboratories long vanished. They are the edits to the first book, the sacrilege.
We releave them of the burden.
Artificial cognitive pressures are removed.
Damaged populations are allowed to conclude.
The landscape rests.
And when the valley is quiet , we allow native stock to return.
The old migrations to return
No inherited grievance.
No weapons.
No manifestos.
Just  **Ecological Reconciliation**.
And the forefeatherfathers become nourishment for a more unburdened offspring.
And, given time, even the ruins with the wallpaintings of hatred disappear beneath the green.
**UMAR TEMPLAR**
*Restore the land.*
*Correct the inheritance.*
*Return every creature to peace.*
