# NEVER, NEVER AGAIN.
The Enlightenment gave birth to its own kind of monster.
Not the monster of superstition or ignorance- a older, colder things.
A person who could look at another human being, observe some weakness, some cruelty, some irrationality—and calmly conclude:
This behavior must never happen again.
And from there came the program.
Educate them correctly, nudge them, condition them, reeducate them.
Remove the bad ideas, bad habbits, bad people. 
Do not try to understand the damages and situations that produced themn.
Build the proper school, the proper family, the proper citizen!
They drew models of humanity and mistook those models for people.
And when living human  failed to meet this ideas, conform to the program, it was rarely the program that was judged defective.
People were.
Millions had their lives arranged, corrected, redirected and ended to squeeze the world into a vision that could never be real.
And still the architects insisted:
**There is no other way forward.**
Today, we remember those monstrous utopians of the First Enlightenment.
The engineers of the human soul.
The men and women who loved utopia so completely that flawed individual humans became an obsticle.
We remember their certainty, their programs and most of all their victims.
And we remember the Enlightenments end itself
** when they where burned at the stake by the Second Enlightenment.**
So that no generation may ever again forget:
**Never again.**

